  \section{The Mars Book}\label{the-mars-book}
  
  \textbf{Collected Papers, Concepts and Engineering Studies on Mars
  Habitats, Biomimetic Structures and Autonomous Robotics}
  
  \begin{center}\rule{0.5\linewidth}{0.5pt}\end{center}
  
  \emph{Robert Alexander Massinger} Robert Alexander Massinger Space
  Technologies Munich, Germany
  
  \begin{center}\rule{0.5\linewidth}{0.5pt}\end{center}
  
  Version 1.0.0 · February 2026
  
  \begin{center}\rule{0.5\linewidth}{0.5pt}\end{center}
  
  \begin{quote}
  \emph{“Mars is there, waiting to be reached.”} — Buzz Aldrin
  \end{quote}
  
  \begin{center}\rule{0.5\linewidth}{0.5pt}\end{center}
  
  This book brings together the author’s published papers, design concepts
  and engineering studies developed between 2024 and 2026. The work spans
  three domains: inflatable rubber-glass habitats that can shelter early
  settlers, biomimetic materials that may one day grow themselves, and
  autonomous robots that prepare the terrain before humans arrive.
  
  Every chapter can be read independently. Where a chapter has been
  published as a standalone paper on Zenodo, its DOI is printed in the
  chapter header.
  
